she was the first female firefighter in  the new york fire department on 9 11.  when the terrorist attack the now  retired firefighter said she knew  exactly what she had to do tamsen fidel  has her story  you know i was one of the lucky ones  on 9 11 i was a survivor and i think  it's important that everybody remember  that it was the greatest rescue effort  on american soil in our history  and it remains to this day two decades  later the memories of september 11th are  still fresh for former firefighter  brenda berkman we're desperately seeking  anyone who might still be alive and you  know it was like working in a field of  razor blades because basically all the  concrete and glass have been pulverized  when the buildings fell down burkman was  off duty september 11 while waiting for  transport to ground zero she and her  fellow firefighters watched the south  tower fall on television when they  arrived in manhattan workman remembers  that all the firefighters on scene were  immediately put to work i want people to  know that we tried our best to find  anything related to anyone that was lost  down here to try and give the family  some kind of peace she worked on side  almost every day in the wake of the  attack by april of 2002 she was one of  only two assigned officers there there's  a lot of  sorrow that i have that's connected with  this place now we're tired workman's  projects all have a connection to the  day we will never forget from  volunteering with other female 9 11  survivors to her art project 36 views of  one world trade center 343 firefighters  were killed in one day and i just want  to repeat that number 343  and 23 new york city police officers and  37 port authority police officers and  countless numbers of other uniformed  folks who  would run here to try and help however  they could this trailblazing firefighter  says it is the resilience and tenacity  of new yorkers including the first  responders and essential workers who  came to the rescue that day and have  continued to give hope throughout the  pandemic we need to honor them we need  to understand  and and commemorate everything that  happened accurately and then we need to  build back better like we have down here  at  the world trade center in lower  manhattan i'm tamsen fidel
 

